{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RAUS2H4mtY6kUbAYZthPff","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-595\"\n3\ttitle = \"LLR-207/TC-205 return and LLR-208/TC-206 amendment: the verdict rows describe every mechanism that now holds them\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 2\n8\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n9\tbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tFour cells, no new mechanism and no regression written: every arm described\n15\tbelow already existed and passed, and only the record was silent. All four of\n16\tthe spec's claims were re-driven on this tree before anything was edited, and\n17\tall four hold.\n18\t\n19\tRETURNED (`Drafted`, this branch's merge mints their adjudication):\n20\t\n21\t- `LLR-207.detail` — the `governing_rev` clause said the walk peels \"any\n22\t  verified refresh it meets\". `_peel_target` has peeled TWO classes since the\n23\t  second disposable-commit class entered the tree. The clause now names both\n24\t  (the station REFRESH, admitted by `refresh_attestation`; the machinery's own\n25\t  ADJUDICATION CLOSE, admitted by `mechanical_close_attestation` against the\n26\t  exact composed subject, a single parent, and a changed-path set wholly under\n27\t  `docs/work/`), the ONE property that admits them rather than two rules — both\n28\t  machine-authored, both moving the tree without the lane changing what it\n29\t  CLAIMS — and the fail-toward-review direction of every arm. The `work_tip`\n30\t  contrast is now explicit instead of implied: `work_tip` calls\n31\t  `refresh_attestation` DIRECTLY rather than through the shared disposable\n32\t  test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path.\n33\t- `LLR-207.code_symbol` — added `mechanical_close_attestation`, an `__all__`\n34\t  export that changes what both readers answer and that `grep` found described\n35\t  by ZERO rows in any requirements registry. `_peel_target` deliberately left\n36\t  out: private, and the two attestation readers are the named surface.\n37\t- `TC-205.method` / `.evidence` — `THE PEEL` enumerated the refresh arm alone.\n38\t  The second class is now stated in the cell's own idiom, the positive and BOTH\n39\t  refusals, and the three already-passing tests that no test case anywhere\n40\t  cited are cited: the positive (which also asserts the close REALLY moved the\n41\t  tree, and drives the two peels COMPOSING), the hand-written-subject refusal,\n42\t  and the reached-outside-`docs/work/` refusal.\n43\t- `TC-205.tier` — `Smoke` -> `Full`, RULED rather than left open, with the\n44\t  basis recorded in `Method`. 8 of the row's 49 citations live in\n45\t  `test_integrate_admission` / `test_integrate_station`, both in\n46\t  `tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES` and so deselected by `-m smoke`. `Full` is\n47\t  the cheapest tier at which the whole cited set runs; `Smoke` claimed\n48\t  commit-floor coverage for a set the commit floor only partly runs, which is\n49\t  the direction §12.2 names as the harmful one. Sibling `TC-132` already reads\n50\t  `Full` while citing the same station module.\n51\t\n52\tAMENDED (Approved cells; §A5.2 mints their amendment adjudication at merge —\n53\tno `Status` was flipped and no `docs/archive/last_approved/` was written):\n54\t\n55\t- `LLR-208.detail` — the cell said regen-set membership \"is the only thing that\n56\t  makes the exclusive-writer clause above true\". That stopped being true when\n57\t  the off-trunk refusal shipped, and the snapshot had copied the claim whole.\n58\t  It now states BOTH mechanisms and keeps them distinct, because they hold\n59\t  different halves and neither substitutes for the other:\n60\t  `_off_trunk_refusal` ENFORCES the clause (exit 2 on any branch but the trunk,\n61\t  keyed on the PRIMARY checkout, with `--trunk-step` the one exempt caller\n62\t  because the station's refresh runs the trunk step inside a lane worktree, and\n63\t  `--check` never refused), while regen-set membership keeps the artifact\n64\t  FRESH. The cell records why the refusal is load-bearing and not\n65\t  belt-and-braces: without it the generator returned 0, wrote the directory in\n66\t  a claimed lane, and the work-branch freshness stand-down HID the write.\n67\t- `LLR-208.code_symbol` — added `_off_trunk_refusal` (the row already names the\n68\t  private `_extra`, so this follows its own convention).\n69\t- `TC-206.method` / `.evidence` — stated the refusal arm, including why it had\n70\t  to be driven through a real LINKED worktree (the single-checkout fixtures\n71\t  every other arm uses are their own trunk and keep writing), and cited its\n72\t  detector.\n73\t\n74\tBar `DevStg-Tests` met and re-driven at the close tip; results in\n75\t`docs/log.d/WI-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr.md`, which also records the two\n76\tdecisions the cells cannot carry themselves (`LLR-208.hat_refs` left unset\n77\tdeliberately, and the `SR-170`/`UNATTENDED-OPS` question surfaced as a separate\n78\tfinding rather than fixed inline). Nothing was widened into the out-of-scope\n79\t`work_tip` docstring defect the spec fenced off.\n80\t\n81\t## Context\n82\t\n83\tDrafted by WI-590 (its ## Dispositions section) and minted at its merge - drafts-not-mints, ruling R1/R3.\n84\t\n85\tVERDICT THIS CONTINUES:\n86\t`docs/reviews/wi-590-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/004-ADJUDICATE-774ef35.md`,\n87\tgoverning line `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=4`. `LLR-208` and `TC-206` were APPROVED by\n88\tthat act; they enter this scope as an AMENDMENT (round 011 MAJOR, below), not\n89\tas a return. NO OVERLAPPING ADJUDICATION REMAINS: `WI-594` (minted at\n90\t`09193fea` for the out-of-band trunk range) was minted naming these four rows\n91\tas well as LLR-209 and TC-207; round 012 drove its first-approval brief and\n92\tfound it would put LLR-207 and TC-205 in front of a fourth adjudicator as\n93\tawaiting first approval, with none of this lane