{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CejNj97axc3V7SnK6dNDj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-595 is closed. Final state on `wi-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr`:\n\n```\n149698f0 record: WI-595 — the closing-tip re-run, and four unmasked nodes\n23cbacfa record: WI-595 — the session record the close commit dropped\n708e8047 close: WI-595 — the verdict rows describe every mechanism that now holds them\n57792a3b spine: LLR-207.detail names the non-empty path-set arm of the close peel\n```\n\n**What I changed beyond the inherited work.** The branch arrived with the four cells largely written. I re-drove every claim rather than trusting it, and found one real defect in the draft: `LLR-207.detail` described the mechanical-close peel as admitting \"a changed-path set lying wholly under `docs/work/`\" — **a clause the empty set satisfies vacuously**. The code (`verdict.py:426`) refuses zero-path commits outright via `if not paths or …`. That matters concretely: the zero-path commit is a real class here (`commit_telemetry` writes one) and `TC-205` already drives it elsewhere. The cell now says NON-EMPTY, and is more precise than the module docstring it describes. I logged the *untested* empty-path arm as a finding rather than writing the regression, since that's outside the spec's stated fence.\n\n**Bar, `DevStg-Tests`.** Full unfiltered suite, run twice as the close is itself an input change:\n- pre-close `57792a3b`: `1 failed, 3383 passed, 25 skipped in 646.97s`\n- closing tip `23cbacfa`: `1 failed, 3387 passed, 21 skipped in 625.67s`\n\nThe single red is the `docs/stage` fingerprint node. It is **caused by this branch and benign** — driven both ways, not argued: passes at the integration base `bd431c5b`, and passes at this tip on a regenerated-stage worktree where every derived field is byte-identical (`drafted` 11, unmoved) and only `fingerprint` moves. I did not regenerate `docs/stage` here; that freshness is the trunk lane's.\n\n**Three things I'd flag for the adjudicator:**\n\n1. **The close commit silently dropped the log fragment.** My `git add` named the pre-move spec path; git refuses the *whole* add on one unmatched pathspec, and I'd sent stderr to `/dev/null`. I caught it from the lingering `M` in `git status` and recovered with a follow-up commit rather than an amend — then *verified* rather than assumed it was free: `governing_identity` is `9cd436be…` at all three commits, so the record commits buy no review round.\n\n2. **A standing expectation was wrong, in the repo's favour.** Closing the last active claim was documented to red `test_the_live_registry_round_trips_in_whichever_home_is_authoritative`. It now passes. The moved counts (25→21 skips) are four `test_wi_convert.py` nodes that stop being masked by the `drained-stop` refusal — I named all four via `-rs` against a pre-close worktree rather than letting a changed count look like a regression.\n\n3. **No approval act was performed.** Verified mechanically: no `docs/archive/last_approved/` write, and **no `status` line added or changed anywhere in the delta**. The four returned cells stay `Drafted`; the two amended Approved cells take their §A5.2 amendment adjudication at merge.\n\nI did not push — `push = \"human\"`. I also corrected two memory entries: the now-fixed drained-tip red, and the `git add` trap."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":139564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b3b322a-5428-4994-a8c4-922ee2b5b80c","uuid":"c0955119-d7eb-4419-ad6c-a34ec8d0a5b2","request_id":"req_011CejNj7ueiCenvsB73C4Gk"}
